{"kind":"artifact","text":"The fold projects the satisfier it bound at admission; workroom-fold@14 unchanged. Exact clean pushed head 6bcb4798e07efe3a8c8de4a495e709520cf099e7 on request/planner-dr-recut; checkout clean, local and origin identical. Successor to fe9013a5 at this path.\n\nTHIS PATH IS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO ITS PREDECESSOR. Neither of my two commits touches internal/workroom: the first changes ui/src, ui/test and the embed, the second changes only comments in internal/app/app_test.go. It is republished so the artifact set stands at one exact head, not because anything here moved.\n\nIT IS NEVERTHELESS THE AUTHORITY THIS HEAD IS JUDGED AGAINST, and the reviewer should read it that way. The browser change at this head is correct only if it mirrors what fold.go actually does, and the two rules it mirrors live here:\n\n  decideState refuses post-genesis state from a signer without the participant\n  role, which is why the state branch of signingRefusal asks isLiveParticipant.\n\n  decideRatify branches on the satisfier bound at admission. The\n  originating-requester branch requires the requester AND f.hasActor, with the\n  comment explaining that a ratified approval is what gs merge consumes so a\n  departed ratifier could still put a head into main. The role:\u003cname\u003e branch\n  requires only f.hasRole and never consults participation.\n\nThat second split is the reason signingRefusal dispatches rather than applying\none predicate. If a later change to decideRatify collapses those branches, the\nbrowser dispatcher becomes wrong in the same motion, and this artifact is the\nedge that should flare when it does.\n\nThe profile advance to @14 is this lane's and is unchanged from 97a749ec: the fold now publishes Statement.Satisfier, so a cache written under @13 lacks the field and is rejected rather than served.\n\nGATES AT THIS EXACT HEAD: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok, zero failures; gofmt clean; go build and go vet exit 0; git diff --check exit 0."